  "snp1.1:7.1": "The commentary interprets <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vitakka</i> as “wrong thoughts”, but the identical line at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/ud6.7/en/sujato#4.1'>Ud 6.7:4.1</a> clearly refers to <i lang='pi' translate='no'>jhāna</i>. The commentary also reads <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vidhūpitā</i> as “burning up”, but <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vidhūpa</i> refers to clearing the mist, smoke, or incense. ",
